(1759555, 236373, 38911, '<td valign="top">Good idea &amp; perspective.  <br/>Nice contrast between the subject &amp; the sky.  <br/>A very interesting photo.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-05 00:19:46.</i></td>', 'Good idea & perspective.  Nice contrast between the subject & the sky.  A very interesting photo.', '2005-10-05 00:43:48.000000', '2005-10-05 01:19:46.000000', 1),
(1759559, 237346, 15711, '<td valign="top">This thumbnail just jumped out at me. The high contrast of blues and reddish browns is just wonderful.  The intensity of color is what landscape photography is all about!  Perfect perspective for the challenge too.</td>', 'This thumbnail just jumped out at me. The high contrast of blues and reddish browns is just wonderful.  The intensity of color is what landscape photography is all about!  Perfect perspective for the challenge too.', '2005-10-05 00:45:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759560, 235359, 36597, '<td valign="top">Great photo... I see the ground, I see the up.... but, when I look at the picture... my eye is drawn down to the left? Good Luck!</td>', 'Great photo... I see the ground, I see the up.... but, when I look at the picture... my eye is drawn down to the left? Good Luck!', '2005-10-05 00:45:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759561, 237290, 15711, '<td valign="top">Ok, this has my heart.  I wish the doggy''s face weren''t in shadow, but this is the cutest thing. The texture of the painted wood adds to the shot. I''d up the sat of cyan to make the sky more vivid. But seeing how my doggy Tank is half chow and I give all animal shots an extra point, this gets a 7. Well, I looked at it again and realized there is no way his face couldn''t be in shadow, as you are looking up at him and unless you are shining a light in his face, it''s gonna be in shadow.  I have thought about this and how much I like it.  Bumping it up to 9 for the composition, clarity and just darn cute shot!!!</td>', 'Ok, this has my heart.  I wish the doggy''s face weren''t in shadow, but this is the cutest thing. The texture of the painted wood adds to the shot. I''d up the sat of cyan to make the sky more vivid. But seeing how my doggy Tank is half chow and I give all animal shots an extra point, this gets a 7. Well, I looked at it again and realized there is no way his face couldn''t be in shadow, as you are looking up at him and unless you are shining a light in his face, it''s gonna be in shadow.  I have thought about this and how much I like it.  Bumping it up to 9 for the composition, clarity and just darn cute shot!!!', '2005-10-05 00:45:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759571, 236650, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is a stunning perspective.  I think I''d have liked it better if part of the area to the left were missing, leaving the misty clouds on the right, and the building wouldn''t be so dead centered in the shot.</td>', 'This is a stunning perspective.  I think I''d have liked it better if part of the area to the left were missing, leaving the misty clouds on the right, and the building wouldn''t be so dead centered in the shot.', '2005-10-05 00:47:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759575, 235059, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is reminiscent of "The Birds," Alfred Hitchcock''s imfamous movie.  I like the use of sepia.</td>', 'This is reminiscent of "The Birds," Alfred Hitchcock''s imfamous movie.  I like the use of sepia.', '2005-10-05 00:48:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759580, 236844, 15711, '<td valign="top">The sky color is delicious! I like the angle of the kid in the swing.  I think I''d like it a tad more if the subjhect weren''t dead centered in the shot.  Maybe alleviate part of the area to the right and it wouldn''t lose any of it''s effectiveness, but actually add to it in my opinion, as the person in the swing wouldn''t have that "bullseye" sense of being right in the middle of the shot.</td>', 'The sky color is delicious! I like the angle of the kid in the swing.  I think I''d like it a tad more if the subjhect weren''t dead centered in the shot.  Maybe alleviate part of the area to the right and it wouldn''t lose any of it''s effectiveness, but actually add to it in my opinion, as the person in the swing wouldn''t have that "bullseye" sense of being right in the middle of the shot.', '2005-10-05 00:50:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759587, 236999, 15711, '<td valign="top">Lovely silhouette against the rich deep colored sky. I like the minimal approach of this shot.  It is effective and soothing. That touch of blue at the top of the photo is wonderful.</td>', 'Lovely silhouette against the rich deep colored sky. I like the minimal approach of this shot.  It is effective and soothing. That touch of blue at the top of the photo is wonderful.', '2005-10-05 00:51:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759590, 235884, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the architecture of this shot.  The browns and blues work in tandem, to create a lovely rich pallette.  All of the lines and crosses are interesting and weave a beautiful image.</td>', 'I like the architecture of this shot.  The browns and blues work in tandem, to create a lovely rich pallette.  All of the lines and crosses are interesting and weave a beautiful image.', '2005-10-05 00:53:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759592, 236183, 15711, '<td valign="top">What a truly beautiful reflection. I don''t see the perspective as much from the ground up, but it is still a stellar capture. Lovely coloration and clarity. 7</td>', 'What a truly beautiful reflection. I don''t see the perspective as much from the ground up, but it is still a stellar capture. Lovely coloration and clarity. 7', '2005-10-05 00:54:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1759594, 237284, 15711, '<td valign="top">Interesting perspective. I like the glow of the four lights.  Lovely sky tones.  On 2nd review, I''m upping my score. 8</td>', 'Interesting perspective. I like the glow of the four lights.  Lovely sky tones.  On 2nd review, I''m upping my score. 8', '2005-10-05 00:55:34.000000', NULL, 1),
