(1759991, 237068, 41897, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Germaine:</b></div><hr/><i> If he was really upside down, his hair wouldn''t be so neat.  It looks as if all you did was rotate a regular snapshot 180 degrees. Really doesn''t fit the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I have never felt compelled to comment on a comment, but this just screamed for me to, so here it is.   <br/>I never tried to indicate that he was upside down.  It is a "from the ground up" challenge.  I rotated nothing, except myself, on the ground, under a swing.  Even the title makes that very clear! How that possibly "really doesn''t fit the challenge" is beyond me.  <br/> <br/>As for the size, I am desperately needing help in that area.  When I reduce it to the maximum allowed pixels it is still far too large a file size.  I don''t know how to change my file size without reducing the image size?????</td>', 'Originally posted by Germaine: If he was really upside down, his hair wouldn''t be so neat.  It looks as if all you did was rotate a regular snapshot 180 degrees. Really doesn''t fit the challenge.   I have never felt compelled to comment on a comment, but this just screamed for me to, so here it is.   I never tried to indicate that he was upside down.  It is a "from the ground up" challenge.  I rotated nothing, except myself, on the ground, under a swing.  Even the title makes that very clear! How that possibly "really doesn''t fit the challenge" is beyond me.   As for the size, I am desperately needing help in that area.  When I reduce it to the maximum allowed pixels it is still far too large a file size.  I don''t know how to change my file size without reducing the image size?????', '2005-10-05 02:35:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1760025, 236988, 30364, '<td valign="top">Your score for this, with more than 150 votes of 5 or less, is a sad indictment of the dismal level of intellectual and imaginative capacity of most DPC voters.  They could not possibly have objected to the technical quality of the image, because it is patently superb.  Therefore, your poor showing can only be because these voters saw no connection with the challenge theme, and/or because it was not a sufficiently ''exciting'' scene.  Pitiful either way.</td>', 'Your score for this, with more than 150 votes of 5 or less, is a sad indictment of the dismal level of intellectual and imaginative capacity of most DPC voters.  They could not possibly have objected to the technical quality of the image, because it is patently superb.  Therefore, your poor showing can only be because these voters saw no connection with the challenge theme, and/or because it was not a sufficiently ''exciting'' scene.  Pitiful either way.', '2005-10-05 02:49:34.000000', NULL, 0),
