(1761109, 236999, 20115, '<td valign="top">How perfect and simply beautiful.  I have such a problem with ideas, what to photo, etc.  I must remember to just keep it simple.  Thank you.</td>', 'How perfect and simply beautiful.  I have such a problem with ideas, what to photo, etc.  I must remember to just keep it simple.  Thank you.', '2005-10-05 11:50:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1761115, 237148, 44172, '<td valign="top">Wow! I was not expecting this to finish so high! I''m super happy about it''s rating! Thanks very, very much to all of those who commented! It''s wonderful to hear the different opinions and receive the feedback in any form!<br/> <br/>Purple sky - UGH! Yes, the sky was meant to be purple. Not sure if I regret that now or not.  I had sooo many different sky versions with this image and ultimately decided on purple because: 1) My little girl loved the purple sky version the most and since I had her input on the title I felt I''d let her help with the color variation also - especially since I was becoming so indecisive about it.  2) The images that I had played with and the different color variations all had a lot of noise in the sky - especially around the pillars themselves, it seemed to me that I had done something (have no idea what) but there seemed to be the least amount of noise in the purple version. 3) And this is strange I know - but I associate the color purple with royalty or regalness, kings &amp; queens etc. - which live in a "castle".<br/> <br/>Thanks again for all the comments - I want to learn as much as I can and all comments (good and bad) are very welcome so I can get an idea of what people really think.   Peace - Shan :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-05 13:52:53.</i></td>', 'Wow! I was not expecting this to finish so high! I''m super happy about it''s rating! Thanks very, very much to all of those who commented! It''s wonderful to hear the different opinions and receive the feedback in any form! Purple sky - UGH! Yes, the sky was meant to be purple. Not sure if I regret that now or not.  I had sooo many different sky versions with this image and ultimately decided on purple because: 1) My little girl loved the purple sky version the most and since I had her input on the title I felt I''d let her help with the color variation also - especially since I was becoming so indecisive about it.  2) The images that I had played with and the different color variations all had a lot of noise in the sky - especially around the pillars themselves, it seemed to me that I had done something (have no idea what) but there seemed to be the least amount of noise in the purple version. 3) And this is strange I know - but I associate the color purple with royalty or regalness, kings & queens etc. - which live in a "castle". Thanks again for all the comments - I want to learn as much as I can and all comments (good and bad) are very welcome so I can get an idea of what people really think.   Peace - Shan :)', '2005-10-05 11:53:50.000000', '2005-10-05 14:52:53.000000', 0),
