(1763870, 236199, 21362, '<td valign="top">Well done on this one, it was one of my favorites in the challenge and I''m glad it placed highly. You did a great job with the black and whites.</td>', 'Well done on this one, it was one of my favorites in the challenge and I''m glad it placed highly. You did a great job with the black and whites.', '2005-10-06 02:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764038, 237050, 7570, '<td valign="top">hi Tiberius, i read your post in the forums, and here is my reply. for me, the photo doesnt really have an interesting spot for my eyes to "feast" upon. when i look at the photo, the eyes rolls all over the photo without any area to pause or capturing my interest. all the time, i''ve been looking at photos mostly by feel. but lately, helpful people have pointed to me things like dynamic range, 9step rules. i think these 2 can greatly enhance a black n white photo such as this. there just isnt enough details in the shadow or higlights (maybe you disagree) but thats just what i felt. i checked your profile, you make great photos, maybe this one just didnt really cut it with the voters.</td>', 'hi Tiberius, i read your post in the forums, and here is my reply. for me, the photo doesnt really have an interesting spot for my eyes to "feast" upon. when i look at the photo, the eyes rolls all over the photo without any area to pause or capturing my interest. all the time, i''ve been looking at photos mostly by feel. but lately, helpful people have pointed to me things like dynamic range, 9step rules. i think these 2 can greatly enhance a black n white photo such as this. there just isnt enough details in the shadow or higlights (maybe you disagree) but thats just what i felt. i checked your profile, you make great photos, maybe this one just didnt really cut it with the voters.', '2005-10-06 04:21:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764139, 236853, 23394, '<td valign="top">you had a great shot, just not a great ''challenge'' shot.  just a little too much for the voters to have to take in.  also, if the overall coloring doesn''t grab you, check it out b/w--that really made the difference for my shot.  you might to also want to check out these shots of bradp''s <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/portfolio.php?USER_ID=19708&amp;collection_id=10801" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>.</td>', 'you had a great shot, just not a great ''challenge'' shot.  just a little too much for the voters to have to take in.  also, if the overall coloring doesn''t grab you, check it out b/w--that really made the difference for my shot.  you might to also want to check out these shots of bradp''s here.', '2005-10-06 07:16:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764192, 235304, 32997, '<td valign="top">Captivating. Well done.</td>', 'Captivating. Well done.', '2005-10-06 08:05:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764398, 237050, 37200, '<td valign="top">You mentioned in the forum post "it''s nothing spectacular".  The question is "what would make it spectacular?" (not that I actually know what I''m talking about).  I think Shadow has a good point...nothing to settle on...it''s a very busy photo.  I think the lighting is one thing that could make a dramatic change in this shot.  It looks like a very bright day, and the tree trunk that is "washed out" kind of draws your attention to it at the egde rather than in for a deeper look at things.  I Can''t tell if this is a flash going off or direct sunlight near the bottom, and shade as you go up.  If it''s sunlight, maybe a reflector to shine up the trunk and onto the leaves would help.</td>', 'You mentioned in the forum post "it''s nothing spectacular".  The question is "what would make it spectacular?" (not that I actually know what I''m talking about).  I think Shadow has a good point...nothing to settle on...it''s a very busy photo.  I think the lighting is one thing that could make a dramatic change in this shot.  It looks like a very bright day, and the tree trunk that is "washed out" kind of draws your attention to it at the egde rather than in for a deeper look at things.  I Can''t tell if this is a flash going off or direct sunlight near the bottom, and shade as you go up.  If it''s sunlight, maybe a reflector to shine up the trunk and onto the leaves would help.', '2005-10-06 10:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764488, 237352, 63, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the great comments.  I''m so happy to finally win a ribbon.  <br/>The photo was the results of an eight mile hike, which I shot around 150 images of the aspen trees from ground level.  No filters were used, the sky is that color blue at 10,000'' elevation.<br/>Thank''s<br/>Jim Sapp</td>', 'Thanks for all the great comments.  I''m so happy to finally win a ribbon.  The photo was the results of an eight mile hike, which I shot around 150 images of the aspen trees from ground level.  No filters were used, the sky is that color blue at 10,000'' elevation.Thank''sJim Sapp', '2005-10-06 11:16:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764573, 234739, 42792, '<td valign="top">This is a really beautiful shot and it''s really a bonus to know there was no post-processing done.  Your photo gives me hope for great original off the camera shots.  Don''t get me wrong.  I''m thankful for software that can do wonders but I do prefer to spend more time taking pictures than tinkering on the image after.  Didn''t vote in this challenge but the fact that you finished in 36 place out of over 300 entries - I''d say that in itself is a tribute to its originality!!!  Very impressive, especially only after 3 challenges!  You should be celebrating. :)</td>', 'This is a really beautiful shot and it''s really a bonus to know there was no post-processing done.  Your photo gives me hope for great original off the camera shots.  Don''t get me wrong.  I''m thankful for software that can do wonders but I do prefer to spend more time taking pictures than tinkering on the image after.  Didn''t vote in this challenge but the fact that you finished in 36 place out of over 300 entries - I''d say that in itself is a tribute to its originality!!!  Very impressive, especially only after 3 challenges!  You should be celebrating. :)', '2005-10-06 12:09:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1764638, 236504, 40977, '<td valign="top">For those who were confused by this image being submitted in the Ground Up challenge, Let me assure you that I was below him looking up.  Two Reasons (that aren''t my word) to support this:<br/>I was laying back on the jetski which you can see in the bottom of his glasses - the red handlebar. The other is that if it was straight on (which I can see that being the assumption, based on the outcome of the shot) I would be smack dab in the middle of his sunglass lens.<br/> <br/>anyhow..just wanted to address this because an overwhelming number of the comments I received was regarding how the image didn''t fit the challenge.  :)</td>', 'For those who were confused by this image being submitted in the Ground Up challenge, Let me assure you that I was below him looking up.  Two Reasons (that aren''t my word) to support this:I was laying back on the jetski which you can see in the bottom of his glasses - the red handlebar. The other is that if it was straight on (which I can see that being the assumption, based on the outcome of the shot) I would be smack dab in the middle of his sunglass lens. anyhow..just wanted to address this because an overwhelming number of the comments I received was regarding how the image didn''t fit the challenge.  :)', '2005-10-06 12:43:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765237, 234739, 44882, '<td valign="top">Hello, <br/> <br/>I did not comment much your photo during the voting, but you should know that yours was the only 10 point I gave during this challenge, I think its a wonderful work. <br/></td>', 'Hello,  I did not comment much your photo during the voting, but you should know that yours was the only 10 point I gave during this challenge, I think its a wonderful work. ', '2005-10-06 16:28:49.000000', NULL, 0),
